Z||000000||1FieroGTRacingInc||10-10-2000||09:35 PM||||I need to tow my mom's Ford Tempo....  I have a chain,BUT ....WHERE do I hoo the chain to my 87GT???  I don't want to bend any part of the cradle or anything...  Any suggestion's??   Thank's for the help...  My mom said Thank You....  I'm wanting her to get a Fiero too...   Maybe someday...  he he he...    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">     Steve ||||reg||5
Z||000001||rprevo||10-10-2000||09:45 PM|||| The best way to prevent bending your cradle is borrow a pick-up truck to tow cars with.<P><BR> Ray<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FieroGTRacingInc||10-10-2000||09:54 PM||||Thank's for the suggestion, But I don't have anyone with a truck tonight.....  I have to do it tonight too.... ALL I have to do it with is my GT...   Steve||||reg||1
Z||000003||Xtreme Fiero's||10-10-2000||10:54 PM||||I realy dont think a tempo will bend the cradle. A concrete wall took a jab at mine (45mph+) and it's still square. make sure the rope dosen't bang up the botom of the trunk or the exhaust though.||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FieroGTRacingInc||10-10-2000||11:02 PM||||Thank's Xtreme.....   So it will be ok to hook it to the cradle....  ?    Steve<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||007DOUG||10-10-2000||11:20 PM||||When I flatbed 84-87 fieros, I hook-up to the slotted hole on each side of the cradle. The holes are directly in front of where the P-brake cables passes through the cradle.<P>I have to install an eyehook in 88's<P>Those two holes keep the rear of the fiero from sliding around........even with the way I drive.<P>------------------<BR>5 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>84 SE<BR>86 SE V6 153K<BR>2 86 GT's<BR>86 GT 3.4 Pearl White T-top<BR>2 88 GT's (twins)<P>However......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FieroGTRacingInc||10-11-2000||01:21 AM||||Thank's Doug...  I'll give it a shot...  ||||reg||1
